# Ignore all Claude CLI personal files and state.
# NB `.claude/*` not `.claude/` — git never descends into an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY,
# so with `.claude/` the four `!` negations below are silently INERT and none of
# these files can be staged. Excluding the directory's CONTENTS instead lets the
# negations work. Verified: `git check-ignore -v .claude/rules/` used to report
# the `.claude/` line as the match. The tell-tale symptom here was that hooks/,
# skills/ and settings.json WERE tracked (force-added past the inert rule) while
# rules/, created later, silently vanished.
.claude/*
# NOT `!.claude/settings.json`: the file hardcodes an absolute, machine- and
# node-version-specific interpreter path (`/home/<user>/.nvm/versions/node/vX/bin/caliber`,
# 4x), so every clone got hooks pointing at a path that does not exist for them.
# It was tracked; this commit untracks it. Make those commands portable before
# tracking it again (the Stop hook already shows how: `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`).
.claude/settings.json
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/hooks/
.opencode/node_modules/
.opencode/memory/
.opencode/.env

vendor
.codenomad
.logs

# Caliber local state
.caliber/

# Test / coverage artifacts
.phpunit.cache/
coverage.xml
coverage-report/
# S305 — the per-case JUnit report the browser-E2E gate reads (CI writes it with
# `--log-junit junit.xml`; it is a build artifact, never committed).
junit.xml
.phpunit.result.cache
# S120 assertion-escape guard report (written only when a run has violations)
.phpunit-assertion-escapes.json

# PHP-DI compiled container
var/cache/

# Installed plugin sources (runtime data, not source)
var/plugins/

# Runtime theme files (extracted from ui-theme plugins)
var/themes/

# Smarty compile cache (created when templates render)
templates_c/

# Admin SPA (admin-ui/) — see step 0.4. Build-output decision: the built
# bundle in public/assets/admin/ IS committed (so the production server has
# no Node build dependency at runtime), but the local dev artifacts are not.
admin-ui/node_modules/
admin-ui/coverage/
admin-ui/.vite/
admin-ui/*.tsbuildinfo
# NB: public/assets/admin/ (the built bundle) is intentionally NOT ignored.

# Transient supervisor handoff docs (Wave-N work notes, intentionally untracked)
